# Test-run isolation, half two of two. Bun loads THIS file natively before
# any JS runs, so its values are baked into the environment bun starts
# with, and that starting environment is what Bun.spawn hands to a child
# by default. tests/isolate-app-settings.ts (loaded via bunfig.toml's
# [test] preload) sets the same variable by mutating process.env, which
# covers code in THIS process reading it directly, but does NOT reach a
# Bun.spawn call with no `env` option: verified on bun 1.3.14 that such a
# runtime assignment to process.env is invisible to that default, because
# it is drawn from the environment bun started with, not the live
# process.env object. Many tests spawn `bun src/cli.ts` with no `env`
# option at all (tests/cli.test.ts, tests/cli-settings.test.ts,
# tests/field-station.test.ts, and others), so this file is the piece that
# actually guards them.
#
# Keep this value identical to tests/isolate-app-settings.ts's. Nothing
# enforces the two agree. A SCREEPUB_CONFIG_DIR already in the real shell
# environment overrides this (dotenv never replaces an already-set
# variable), so a developer pointing it somewhere on purpose is respected.
SCREEPUB_CONFIG_DIR=/dev/null/screepub-test-guard
